---
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="Why a Ph.D. dropout in physics writes about mathematics from first principles, and the questions behind this site."
  activeSection="about"
>
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />

  <article class="prose page-prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p style="margin-top: 1.4em;">
      I was pursuing a Ph.D. in physics, and I dropped out of the program.
    </p>
    <p>
      What stayed with me was how I like to learn: from first principles. I was never satisfied with just being handed a formula. I wanted to know why the dot product is defined the way it is, why the cross product is defined the way it is, and how the trigonometric identities are derived.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is where I work through those questions, one step at a time, so that each result feels inevitable rather than memorized.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
